<.shell title="Buttons and tags" current={:components}>
  <h1>Buttons and tags</h1>
  <p class="lead">Flat buttons with a hard bottom edge, and small tags for status.</p>

  <h2>Button kinds</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="actions">
      <button class="btn">Save settings</button>
      <button class="btn secondary">Cancel</button>
      <button class="btn success">Create letter</button>
      <button class="btn danger">Delete clause</button>
      <button class="btn link">More information</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Primary</strong>: the one main action on a page.</li>
    <li><strong>Secondary</strong>: everything else, including Cancel and Reset.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Success</strong>: an action that creates or adds, where green helps scanning a table.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Danger</strong>: deletes or removes. Ask first when it cannot be undone.</li>
    <li><strong>Link</strong>: a quiet action inside text or beside other buttons.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Sizes</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="actions">
      <button class="btn">Default, md text</button>
      <button class="btn sm">Small, sm text</button>
      <button class="btn sm secondary">Small secondary</button>
      <button class="btn sm success">Create letter</button>
      <button class="btn sm danger">Remove</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    Default is 36px tall for forms and page actions. Small is 24px, for table rows and toolbars.
  </p>

  <h2>States</h2>
  <p>
    Every kind in every state, frozen so you can compare them on any screen. Try the real ones
    above: on a phone, press and hold to see the pressed state.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="btn-states">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Kind</th>
          <th>Default</th>
          <th>Hover</th>
          <th>Pressed</th>
          <th>Focus</th>
          <th>Disabled</th>
          <th>Busy</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr :for={{kind, label} <- button_kinds()}>
          <td>{label}</td>
          <td><button class={["btn", kind]}>Save</button></td>
          <td><button class={["btn", kind, "is-hover"]} tabindex="-1">Save</button></td>
          <td><button class={["btn", kind, "is-active"]} tabindex="-1">Save</button></td>
          <td><button class={["btn", kind, "is-focus"]} tabindex="-1">Save</button></td>
          <td><button class={["btn", kind]} disabled>Save</button></td>
          <td>
            <button class={["btn", kind]} disabled>
              <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span> Saving…
            </button>
          </td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Hover</strong> darkens the button, only on devices with a mouse or trackpad.</li>
    <li><strong>Pressed</strong> drops the button 2px onto its edge, on every device.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Focus</strong>
      is yellow with a dark edge for every kind, so keyboard users see one signal.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Disabled</strong> is a last resort. Prefer an error that says what is missing.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Busy</strong> shows a spinner and says what it is doing, for work that takes more
      than a second.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Button rows</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="actions">
      <button class="btn">Save settings</button>
      <button class="btn secondary">Cancel</button>
      <button class="btn danger push">Delete team</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">The main action first. A destructive action sits apart, on the right.</p>

  <h2>Tags</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="actions">
      <span class="tag">Draft</span>
      <span class="tag primary">Primary</span>
      <span class="tag success">Qualified</span>
      <span class="tag warning">Expires in 12 days</span>
      <span class="tag danger">Not invited</span>
      <span class="tag info">Synced</span>
    </div>
    <div class="actions">
      <span class="tag incident">Incident</span>
      <span class="tag exercise">Exercise</span>
      <span class="tag event">Event</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    Status tags are tinted; D4H activity tags are solid, matching D4H. Tags are labels, not
    buttons: nothing happens when you click one.
  </p>

  <h2>Focus</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <p>
      Press Tab. Everything you can reach gets the yellow focus, the same in both modes: <a href="#">a link</a>, <button class="btn sm">a button</button>, and
      <input type="text" class="input-sm" style="width: 160px" aria-label="An input" />.
    </p>
  </div>
</.shell>
